bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    seed_jit_erased_float_arg_heap_box_per_call_never_released_2026-11-27, 0, "Measured (base seed aa542919a298e130, aarch64, JIT): fn g(x) -> i64 with a Some/None match, called 4e7 times as g(a) + g(b) with val a: f64 = 1.5 takes 31.6s and 1.3 GB max RSS (an i64 or parse_int argument: 0.2s, 41 MB). Each f64 crossing an erased parameter is BoxFloat'd (rt_value_float heap-allocates a HeapFloat, tracked as transient) and nothing frees it during the loop. seed_jit_erased_f64_option_some_binds_raw_bits_2026-11-27's boundary conversion pays the same per-call box for f64? Some arguments."

